# Line endings. See README §"Windows: the CRLF trap".
#
# Git's Windows default (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout.
# That breaks BOTH deliverables in this repo, and the second failure is silent:
#
#   1. setup-claude-code.sh — bash reads `set -euo pipefail\r` and dies with
#      ": invalid option name" plus "line 58: $'\r': command not found".
#   2. setup-payload-*.tar.gz.b64 — `base64 -d` rejects the stray \r, so the
#      payload never unpacks. This one only surfaces AFTER the script is fixed.
#
# Verified 2026-08-31 on a fresh Windows clone: all four tracked text files came
# out CRLF and the installer could not run.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh  text eol=lf
*.py  text eol=lf
*.md  text eol=lf

# Payloads are base64 streams, not prose: never touch a byte of them.
*.b64 -text
